{"id":"8c12c8e2e9f340908164d4aab9355e28","owner":"ACTmapi","ownerId":"162f854441ae3636a4bab60783daddec","orgId":"E5n4f1VY84i0xSjy","created":1714360647000,"modified":1774834123000,"guid":null,"name":"ACTGOV_Contours_2m","title":"ACTGOV Contours 2m","type":"Vector Tile Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Service","Vector Tile Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:12pt;'>This 2m contours of the ACT as vector tile was derived from 1m AHD (Australian Height Datum) DEM (Digital Elevation Model) from LiDAR (2020). 1m AHD DEM tiles were mosaicked and resampled using Bilinear Interpolation. Then it was smoothed using ESRI ArcGIS Pro 3.1 <a href='https://pro.arcgis.com/en/pro-app/latest/help/analysis/raster-functions/contour-function.htm' style='color:rgb(0, 97, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Adaptive Smoothing<\/a>. Contours were created using the Contour (Spatial Analyst) tool with base height of 550m with 2m intervals. Subsequent steps below were taken to generalise and improve web display:<\/p><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><ul><li><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;'>Generalised output features using the Douglas-Peucker algorithm with a 0.06m tolerance.<\/span><\/li><li><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;'>Split features every 2000 vertices<\/span><\/li><li><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;'>Validated geometries against OGC Simple Feature Access 1.2 specification.<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div style='font-family:inherit;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:medium;'>The vector tile format was created for use in the ACTmapi's Survey Infrastructure web application to support performance. <\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["ACTmapi","Survey","Positioning","Elevation","GDC_0B1360DF"],"snippet":"2m contours of the ACT as vector tile in MGA2020\n.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[148.73397836878362,-35.93358403658224],[149.43833459223973,-35.110832244892634]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"7855","accessInformation":"Australian Capital Territory","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/' style='color:rgb(0, 97, 155); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Creative Commons By Attribution 4.0<\/a> (Australian Capital Territory)<\/p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='color:rgb(0, 0, 31); letter-spacing:-0.05pt;'>Please read <\/span><a href='https://www.actmapi.act.gov.au/terms-and-conditions' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Data Terms and Conditions<\/a><span style='color:rgb(0, 0, 31); letter-spacing:-0.05pt;'> statement before data use.<\/span><\/p>","culture":"en-au","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://tiles.arcgis.com/tiles/E5n4f1VY84i0xSjy/arcgis/rest/services/ACTGOV_Contours_2m/VectorTileServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":613391021,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"commentsEnabled":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews